   "resumo_en": "Hooker 'n Heat is a double album released by blues musician John Lee Hooker and the band Canned Heat in early 1971.\nIt was the first of Hooker's albums to chart, reaching number 73 on the Billboard 200 chart. Hooker plays unaccompanied on side one and \"Alimonia Blues\"; on the remainder of side two and \"The World Today\" and \"I Got My Eyes on You\" Hooker is accompanied by Alan Wilson on various instruments. The full band plays with Hooker on the rest of side three and all of side four.\nThe song \"Whiskey and Wimmen\" was released as a single.",
