   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reheated",
   "resumo_en": "Reheated is the twelfth album by American blues rock band Canned Heat, released in 1988. It features two members of the band's classic lineup, Fito de la Parra and Larry Taylor. Among the titles, \"Bullfrog Blues\" was originally on the B-side of the first single recorded by Canned Heat in 1967; \"Built for Comfort\" by Willie Dixon was popularized by Howlin' Wolf; \"Take Me to the River\" is an R&B/soul song which has been recorded by artists such as Al Green and Talking Heads.\n\"Bullfrog Blues\", \"Mercury Blues\" and \"Take Me To The River\" had been part of the setlist on the previous tour, as heard on Boogie Up The Country from 1987.",
